# No environment variables yet — this skeleton ships with no server secrets
# and no client-visible config. When a real project needs one:
#
# - A server secret goes here, is read through $env/dynamic/private, and
#   never reaches the browser.
# - A PUBLIC_ variable is inlined into the client bundle. Never give one a
#   name that reads as a token, secret or key — scripts/gates.sh fails the
#   build if it sees PUBLIC_*_TOKEN / PUBLIC_*_SECRET / PUBLIC_*_KEY.
#
# For local development: `vercel link`, then `vercel env pull .env.local`.
# That writes real values into .env.local, which is gitignored. Don't copy
# this file to .env and fill it in by hand — pulling keeps it current.
